2026-09-27T07:22:14.9486242Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9486430Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9486702Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9486950Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9487044Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9487245Z ================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9487373Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9487522Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9487872Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9488075Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9488178Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9488436Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9488604Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9488731Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9489107Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9489476Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9490401Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9490869Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9491060Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9491459Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9491942Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9492193Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9492498Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9492862Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9492945Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9493331Z ========
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9493439Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9494566Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9495739Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9495938Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9496371Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9497153Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9497685Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9498201Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9498595Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9498827Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9499037Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9499268Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9499408Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9500588Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9501608Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9502187Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9502970Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:22:14.9503166Z 
